--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Lazy-wave cable on a graded mesh in a cross current: a mesh-scale compression is no grounded-run limit
-- The lazy wave of lazy_wave_touchdown_planar_coarse_att.dat (25 discrete buoyancy modules on a
-- frictional seabed) with its buoyant stretch refined fourfold, so 0.9 m elements meet 4 m ones at
-- the sag bend and 10 m ones along the grounded run, in a 0.2 m/s current across the line's plane.
-- The catenary-continuation route stops on an element-mean axial compression read on those long
-- elements, where the axial force of a stiff line oscillates: a mesh artefact, not the friction
-- holding the grounded run. The static solve names it as such and goes on to the mesh-sequenced
-- route, which solves the deck.
